    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.is_matching - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.is_matching.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.is_matching()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Check if a set of edges forms a valid matching.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.is_matching()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Check if a set of edges forms a valid matching.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.is_matching()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Check if a set of edges forms a valid matching.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nCheck if a set of edges forms a valid matching.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L77379-L77474){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.is_matching(edges)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Is matching](../assets/graphs/is-matching.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"The same two-by-three ladder on both sides, with the candidate edges in the accent color. Left: A-D, B-C, and E-F touch six different nodes, so is_matching() returns True. Right: B-C and C-F both end at C (filled in the accent color), so is_matching() returns False.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nA matching is a set of edges where no two edges share a common endpoint (node). In other\nwords, each node is \"used\" by at most one selected edge. Matchings model one-to-one\npairings: workers to tasks, students to projects, donors to recipients, or any situation\nwhere each item can be paired with at most one partner.\n\nThis method validates a candidate set of edges, which is useful for:\n\n- checking a hand-built or externally computed pairing before acting on it\n- sanity-checking the output of `maximal_matching()` or similar algorithms\n- enforcing a \"no shared endpoints\" constraint while building a pairing incrementally\n\nThe check visits the edges in order and returns `False` as soon as an edge touches a node\nalready used by an earlier edge. Edge direction is ignored (`A -> B` uses both `A` and\n`B`). Listing the same edge ID twice counts as a conflict, and an empty list is a valid\n(empty) matching.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[edges]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [list[Union[int, str]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   A list of integer edge IDs to check, such as values from `get_edge_ids()` or the\n    output of `maximal_matching()`. Edge labels and other strings are not accepted. If any\n    ID does not correspond to an edge in the graph, the method returns `False`.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   `True` if the edges exist and form a valid matching (no shared endpoints), `False`\n    otherwise.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~maximal_matching`) \n\n:   A matching that no edge can be added to.\n\n[](`~is_maximal_matching`) \n\n:   Check that no edge can be added to a matching.\n\n[](`~is_perfect_matching`) \n\n:   Check that a matching pairs every node.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nTwo separate edges share no node, so they form a matching. In a path, the two edges\nmeet at `B`, so they don't:\n\n::: {#3735b385 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\npairs = ec.Graph.from_edges([(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"C\", \"D\")])\npath = ec.Graph.from_edges([(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\")])\n\n(\n    pairs.is_matching(pairs.get_edge_ids()),\n    path.is_matching(path.get_edge_ids()),\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n(True, False)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nAn empty list is a matching too, with no pairs:\n\n::: {#a0162e7a .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\npath.is_matching([])\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\nTrue\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Checking a draft assignment\n\n`teams()` links the 8 workers of a made-up software team to the 8 tasks of a release that\neach can do, weighted by the hours it would take them. A manager's first draft gives Priya\nand Tom the Backend task both, which isn't a matching. Moving Tom to Frontend fixes it:\n\n::: {#387321a0 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nteam = ec.teams()\ndraft = {\n    \"Priya\": \"Backend\", \"Tom\": \"Backend\", \"Mei\": \"Design\",\n    \"Omar\": \"Database\", \"Sara\": \"Docs\", \"Kofi\": \"Security\",\n    \"Hana\": \"Testing\",\n}\n\ndef edges(plan):\n    return [team.find_edge_ids(w, t)[0] for w, t in plan.items()]\n\nfixed = {**draft, \"Tom\": \"Frontend\"}\nteam.is_matching(edges(draft)), team.is_matching(edges(fixed))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```\n(False, True)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#fa9b9b6b .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nteam.layout_bipartite(align=\"horizontal\", aspect_ratio=0.4).plot(\n    layout=\"pos\", highlight_edges=edges(fixed), label_by=\"label\",\n    height=300,\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</style>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"700\" heigh